{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Hey, come on in. I'm just gonna grab a few numbers before the doctor steps over.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Oh sure, yeah. Umm, the parking lot was a nightmare, some guy in a truck took like ten minutes to back out. Anyway.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): Pulse is 118, blood pressure one thirty eight over 82, temp 37.1 celsius, sats 99 percent. Sorry if I seem foggy, my little guy had an earache all night and I barely slept.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Aw, poor kid. This isn't a kid thing, I just feel weird. Dana came with me, she kind of keeps me on track.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'm Dr. Shah. What brought you in today?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): So, umm, I keep losing weight and my heart's been racing. Like I'll be sitting on the couch watching that baking show and boom, it's pounding. And I...",
  "[SEG0007] person_4 (CAREGIVER): Sorry, she asked me to jump in if she wanders. She's been soaking through shirts too.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah yeah the sweating. And my hands shake when I try to, uh, pour coffee. I eat way more than I used to, which is the weird part, and still the weight just...",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (DOCTOR): Still dropping. When did the weight loss start?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Oh man, dates. We went to that food truck festival, the one with the terrible parking, and I had two arepas and still wanted...",
  "[SEG0011] person_4 (CAREGIVER): That was spring. She's not answering you.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Right, sorry. The weight thing, last winter, or the one before. I honestly can't pin it down.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (DOCTOR): Okay, so the timing is fuzzy. Any chest pain with the racing heart?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No chest pain. It just goes fast.",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (DOCTOR): Shortness of breath?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm. I can breathe fine. I walked up from the garage no problem, except I was sweaty.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any fever?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): No fever. I checked a couple times 'cause Dana made me.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any issues peeing, burning or going more often?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Nope. Pee's normal. Of. Sorry, normal.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (DOCTOR): And the bowels, any diarrhea?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): No diarrhea. I just get hungry. Like second breakfast hungry, second lunch. There was this taco place...",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (DOCTOR): We'll stay with the hunger. Are you on any medicines?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm, Mizartan for the pressure. I think it's forty milligrams, once a day. And Omprazole, 20 milligrams every morning, for the heartburn. I don't miss those. And there was something else, err...",
  "[SEG0025] person_4 (CAREGIVER): That's not hers. I take Metformine, 500, for my own sugar. Don't put that on her chart. Her Mizartan she does take, I see the bottle.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah what I was gonna say wasn't a medicine, it was the, uh, the pill box Dana got me. Pink, from the dollar store. Anyway.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (DOCTOR): Anyone in the family with thyroid trouble?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): My sister. She has a thyroid thing, they told her Graves. She lives in Ohio, we argue about Thanksgiving every year, it's a whole...",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (DOCTOR): Got it, sister with Graves. Do you smoke, or drink?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Never smoked. I'll have a beer on the weekend, that's it. I work at the bike shop on Pine, which is funny 'cause I'm dropping weight without even riding.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): Let me look at your hands and your neck. There's a fine tremor in both hands, pulse is regular but fast, matching that 118, and the thyroid feels a little full. Eyes aren't bulging.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Full like swollen? Is that bad? My neighbor's cat had a swollen...",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (DOCTOR): An overactive thyroid pumps out extra hormone that revs the metabolism. The body burns calories even while you eat more, the heart gets driven faster, and the hands shake. The sweating rides along with that.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (DOCTOR): Let me say it back: weight coming off, eating more, heart racing, sweating, shaky hands, sister with Graves, on Mizartan and Omprazole, no chest pain, no fever, no diarrhea. My working impression is hyperthyroidism, provisional until the labs are back. Anxiety can look a lot like this, so it stays on the list, but losing weight while eating more pushes me toward the thyroid.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay. Umm. So not the tacos.",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (DOCTOR): Not the tacos. I'm ordering thyroid blood tests, TSH and free T4, today. And an ECG while you're here, because of the fast heart rate.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (NURSE): I can run the ECG in the side room after this, and the lab will draw the bloods. We've got a slot.",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (DOCTOR): Good, both are booked. Cut back on caffeine for now, it can poke the heart rate. If you get chest pain, or you faint, go to the ER.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (PATIENT): I do like my afternoon coffee. Like, a large. But okay, I'll ease off.",
  "[SEG0040] person_4 (CAREGIVER): I'll hide the good beans if I have to. That's me being bossy, not a medical thing.",
  "[SEG0041] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'd like to see you back in one week, once those results are in. Front desk will book it.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): A week. Cool. Can I still go to the bike shop thing on Saturday, it's not clinical, there's a raffle for a helmet, dumb prize but...",
  "[SEG0043] person_3 (DOCTOR): Saturday's fine. Just the caffeine and the safety stuff we said.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): Alright. Thanks. Dana, you driving? I left my, uh, never mind."
 ],
